BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (Sixteen-bit entries are straightforward and small, but the number of available data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (clusters is bounded. Larger disk capacities require larger cluster sizes, increasing slack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (for small files. The root-directory limit is an independent problem on FAT16. The central) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (allocation table can become a metadata hotspot and file fragmentation increases chain-walk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (costs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (FAT16's widespread adoption stemmed from bootability, a simple interchange format and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (very large software installed base. It lacks Unix ownership and link semantics,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (original-case Unicode name support without VFAT, native snapshots and crash-durable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (transactions. Recovery success is strongly dependent on the consistency of multiple pieces) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (of metadata.) Tj ET
